<title>USA: Kewaunee Scientific Q4 shr $0.18 vs $0.02.</title>
<headline>Kewaunee Scientific Q4 shr $0.18 vs $0.02.</headline>
<dateline>STATESVILLE, N.C. 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Period ended April 30</p>
<p>				1997			1996</p>
<p> Shr			  $0.18		    $0.02</p>
<p> Net			    421			 56</p>
<p> Revs			14,916		   13,907</p>
<p> Avg shrs		   2,366		    2,367</p>
<p>		 Year</p>
<p> Shr			  $0.96		    $0.15</p>
<p> Net			  2,263			361</p>
<p> Revs			61,961		   57,559</p>
<p> Avg			  2,366		    2,367</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>NOTES: Full company name is Kewaunee Scientific Corp.</p>
<p>The company said rise in sales due to higher prices and increased market penetration.</p>
<p>Income was affected by higher prices, higher sales volume and lower manufacturing costs.</p>
<p>The company recorded a tax benefit of $97,000 for fiscal 1997 resulting from its elimination of its valuation allowance on deferred tax assets.</p>
